---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | BarcodeNest" description="How BarcodeNest handles account, authentication, and API usage information.">
  <article class="narrow legal">
    <div class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</div><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p><strong>Last updated: August 2026</strong></p>
    <h2>Registration</h2><p>Registration collects your name and email address. If you continue with Google or GitHub, we also store the provider name and its durable account identifier so future sign-ins reach the correct BarcodeNest account. To enforce the one-Free-account policy, we store a one-way keyed hash of the registration network address while the account exists; the raw address is not stored in this registration record. We use this information to create and administer API access, provide support, enforce quotas, and protect the service from abuse.</p>
    <h2>Authentication</h2><p>Passwords are stored as one-way Argon2id hashes. OAuth-only accounts do not have a BarcodeNest password. Account-session records support login, token rotation, security monitoring, and logout; raw passwords are never stored.</p>
    <h2>API access</h2><p>Operational records include API-key identifiers, request counts, quota usage, and security logs needed to provide and protect the service. Raw API keys are shown once; BarcodeNest stores a cryptographic digest rather than the raw key.</p>
    <h2>Product data</h2><p>Initial grocery data is derived from Open Food Facts. BarcodeNest provides an indexed API service layer and does not claim ownership of Open Food Facts data.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2><p>For privacy questions, email <a href="mailto:support@barcodenest.com"><u>support@barcodenest.com</u></a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
